==English==

===Etymology===
English form of {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|Aemilia|lang=la}}, a [[gens]] name from {{term|aemulus||[[rival]], or those in the next valley|lang=la}}.
* Emily has been used as a vernacular form of the Germanic [[Amelia]], up to the nineteenth century.

===Proper noun===
{{infl|en|proper noun}} (''plural'' '''Emilys'''<!--this is correct-->)

# {{given name|female}}.

====Related terms====
* [[emulate]] (from the same Latin root)
* [[Emil]], [[Emile]]
* [[Em]], [[Emmie]], [[Emmy]], [[Millie]], [[Milly]] 

